-- System > Class > Record > Field. Only classes with records in the shipped tables; 32-bit floats and ints and one-byte
-- on/off flags, not hashes, handles, srids, enums or bitfields.
-- { "class", { "path", ... }, system = "...", ints = { n, ... }, arr = { "list[].path", ... } }
-- ints: positions in the path list that are whole numbers, so a write can use the right type (a zero reads as both).
-- arr: the same kind of field inside a list. Replace [] with an index, 0 first, up to :array_size(). A # at the end marks a whole number, a ? a flag.
-- flags: on/off fields, one byte.
